  "consequence_for_the_design": "the comparator a learned cost-minimising controller must beat is a single threshold on the discovery step, which is not a learning problem at all. Any pilot that spends training budget must therefore be judged against that rule first, and if the rule already holds task effect at its own budget level, a learned controller is only worth running where the rule cannot go: per-target decisions under loss, or an operating point tight enough that reporting early and reporting late differ.",
